for some sports gamblers betting on the  super bowl coin toss is about as good as  the odds can get but for jim mackinville  the houston furniture mogul known as  mattress mac putting down multi-million  dollar bets on big games is actually a  win-win move  for years mackenville who owns the  three-story chain gallery furniture has  made headline-grabbing wagers as  sensible hedges against his big sales  promotions during big events like the  super bowl march madness or the world  series mack will place a giant bet on  one team and offer customers a full  refund if they win for example during  this year's ncaa men's basketball  tournament mattress mac bet 5.5 million  dollars on the kansas jayhawks and ran a  promotion to refund anyone who spent  three thousand dollars or more on  certain types of mattresses and  furniture if they won which they did the  promotions and beds have helped  mackenville grow the business which he  started with his wife linda in 1981. in  2019 gallery furniture had 164 million  dollars in revenue and by the end of  last year sales grew by about 40  to more than 230 million dollars the  economics of mackinville's strategy has  mostly paid off  during his march madness promotion he  bet a total of 9.86 million dollars  across four bets and won 13.5 million  dollars  gallery furniture sold a total of 12.9  million dollars during that time and  after refunding all of his customers he  had over five hundred thousand dollars  in profit  mattress mac says the promotions also  attract a deep pocketed and more  credit-worthy clientele during the super  bowl customers spent an average of 5 800  and during march madness the business  brought in 842 new customers and  1234 repeat customers  the new ones spent an average of six  thousand seven hundred and sixty four  dollars and the repeats spent an average  of five thousand eight hundred and  eighty two dollars  the percentage of customers who get  approved for in-store financing also  jumps about 10 during sports sales  events but these wagers have not always  been smooth  in 2014 mattress max suffered his  biggest loss when he offered a promotion  that would give customers whatever they  bought for free if the denver broncos  beat the seattle seahawks in that year's  super bowl he did not hedge the  promotion with anything and when seattle  won the business was out nine million  dollars  in the years since he's learned to  always hedge his big sales with a giant  bet and he'll also wager more if sales  are surpassing his potential win total  [Music]  you
 

